## Phase 6 — WebOnOne `users_roles` migration

**Goal:** Single permission table per [05-webonone-users-roles.md](./05-webonone-users-roles.md).

| Task | Paths |
|------|-------|
| Migration | `webonone-v2/backend/migrations/*_users_roles.ts` |
| User role repo | `webonone-v2/backend/src/repositories/userRole.repository.ts` |
| Refactor company repo/service | `company.repository.ts`, `company.service.ts` |
| Super-admin middleware | `requireSuperAdmin.ts` |
| Seed | `seedSuperAdmin.ts`, `env.ts`, `.env.example` |
| Rule doc | `.cursor/rules/webonone-v2-project.mdc` (table names) |

**Exit criteria:** Migration up succeeds; APIs unchanged externally; super-admin check uses `users_roles`.

**Verify:** `npm run migrate -w @webonone/webonone-backend` then `npm run type-check -w webonone-v2-root`

---

## Cross-service integration

- UI Kit stays data-agnostic; consumers implement `LoadUsersFn`.
- `users_roles.user_id` is Identity copy only — no Identity DB queries.
- Email `syncUserRole` calls unchanged.

